          "excerpt": "# Multivariable calculus in Litex, setting-first.\n#\n# Included: a quadratic scalar field, exact coordinate difference quotients,\n# epsilon-delta partial derivatives, and its coordinate gradient.\n#\n# Main line: a scalar field -> exact coordinate difference quotients -> gradient.\n\nhave fn quadratic_surface(p cart(R, R)) R = p(1)^2 + p(2)^2\nhave fn quadratic_gradient(p cart(R, R)) cart(R, R) = (2 * p(1), 2 * p(2))\n\n# Holding y fixed reduces the x-coordinate quotient to a difference of squares.\nthm quadratic_surface_x_difference_quotient:\n    ? forall p cart(R, R), x R:\n        x != p(1)\n        ="
